      "title": "CDD - NUTS level 2",
      "description": "Cooling Degree Day (CDD) index is a weather-based technical index designed to describe the need for the heating energy requirements of buildings. HDD is derived from meteorological observations of air temperature, interpolated to regular grids at 25 km resolution for Europe. Calculated gridded HDD is aggregated and subsequently presented on NUTS-2 level. [Source: This metadata record was automatically extracted from the GeoNode portal eurac]",
